  "coverage_guards": [
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "definitions"
      ],
      "reason": "A block is named by its last label, or by its type when it has none. HCL itself does not say which label is the address: resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"assets\" is referred to as aws_s3_bucket.assets, but data \"aws_ami\" \"ubuntu\" as data.aws_ami.ubuntu, so for a data block the segment a reference resolves against is the first label and not the one declared here. Which label is the address is the tool's rule, not the language's."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "definitions"
      ],
      "reason": "A value is carried with its setting only when it is a scalar literal or a quoted template. An object, a tuple, a heredoc, a function call, a conditional or a for-expression is stated by the entries, calls and references inside it, so asking what such a setting is set to returns those and not its text."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "references"
      ],
      "reason": "A traversal is stated by its first segment only: var.region, local.prefix, module.network and aws_s3_bucket.assets all name what they refer to there. A deeper segment is an attribute read of whatever was addressed, and stating it would link every .arn or .id to any attribute of that name anywhere in the repository."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "definitions",
        "references",
        "calls"
      ],
      "reason": "Nothing is evaluated. Interpolation, conditionals, functions, for-expressions and variable inputs are stated as they were written, so the effective value of a setting, the set of blocks a count or for_each produces, and the file a module source resolves to all depend on inputs this file does not contain."
    }
  ],
  "legacy_rules": []
